# AI Verification

Pre-accept checks for any Cursor-produced code, rule, or plan edit. Cite `@ai-verification.mdc` in prompts when reviewing diffs before merge.

## Facts to verify

- Every cited file path exists (`Read`/`Grep`) before applying a diff
- Package/SDK versions cited match `pubspec.lock`
- Referenced route paths appear in `lib/routing/app_router.dart`
- Dataset field names appear in `assets/data/schema/*.json`
- Test counts claimed match `flutter test` output
- Suggestions touching `parallel-agents.mdc` forbidden shared surface become serial-merge patch notes, not direct edits on per-plan branches

## Categories to tag when a suggestion was wrong

- `api-hallucination` — invented API, endpoint, or SDK method
- `wrong-version` — package or Flutter/Dart version mismatch vs lockfile
- `wrong-path` — file, route, or import path that does not exist
- `stale-docs` — README, rule, or comment contradicts landed code
- `scope-drift` — suggestion outside plan or product boundaries
- `dataset-drift` — model or UI assumes fields/types the dataset does not have
- `security-miss` — nginx, CSP, secrets, or deploy guardrail overlooked

## Cross-references

- `parallel-agents.mdc` — forbidden shared files and serial-merge protocol
- `flo-compass-data.mdc` — dataset topology and session-count guardrails
